@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s48-area-order`
IMPORT `ito-s48a-foreign-worker-regs`
IMPORT `ito-il28-routing`
IMPORT `ito-il28-test-people`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-28 tests: s 48A and the foreign worker Regulations of 5775-2014, with the Foreign Workers Law s 1.
--
-- Every expected value below was worked by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the code was run; the arithmetic is
-- in the comment beside it. A failing assertion is a finding: none has been edited to match the code.
-- The sentences relied on (REG = the Regulations; line numbers are the deposited file's):
--   REG 3(a) (line 30): a caring-sector legal foreign worker: points under ss 34, 36 and 36A, on income under s 2(1) or (2).
--   REG 3(a1) (line 31): any other legal foreign worker: one point under s 34.
--   REG 3(b) (line 32): a legal foreign WOMAN who is not in the caring sector: half a point under s 36A.
--   REG 3(c) (line 33): a stay in part of the tax year: one twelfth of the points for each month of the stay.
--   REG 3(d) (line 34): the provisions of Chapter Three, except as stated in the Regulations, do not apply.
--   REG 4 (line 37): the Regulations apply to income produced in the tax year 2015 or after.
-- s 34 gives 2, s 36 gives 1/4, s 36A gives 1/2 (to a woman).
-- Lettering of readings: A first listed, B second, D declined (ito-il28-test-people.l4).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — s 48A and the Regulations of 5775-2014`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total` t `under` r MEANS `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s34` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 34 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s36` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 36 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s36A` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 36A in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s37` t `under` r MEANS `the points under section 37 in place of the ordinary section for` t `, under` r

§§ `Who is reached`

-- FWL s 1 (line 34): a foreign worker is a worker who is not an Israeli citizen or a resident of Israel.
-- REG 1 (line 17): and who holds a visa under s 2 of the Entry into Israel Law or needs one.
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident`
-- Being an Israeli resident for income tax does not stop him being a foreign worker (s 48A: "אף אם רואים אותו כתושב").
#ASSERT `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` `an Israeli citizen who works in Israel`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` `a worker who is a resident of Israel under the Foreign Workers Law`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` `a person who is not a worker`
-- A foreign worker within s 48A who needs no visa is outside the Regulations' definition.
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is a foreign worker within section 48A` `a foreign man who needs no visa`
#ASSERT NOT `the Regulations reach the taxpayer as a foreign worker` `a foreign man who needs no visa`
-- REG 2: legal = stay and employment permitted, not an expert or guest lecturer, a B/1 visa and licence.
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` `a foreign man with a B/1 visa whose stay is not permitted by law`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` `a foreign man who is an expert from abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker` `a foreign man who holds no B/1 visa`
-- REG 1: caring sector = legal + a caring-sector permit + the stay extended under s 3A(b); both limbs.
#ASSERT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` `a legal foreign man with a caring-sector permit whose stay is not extended, an Israeli resident`
#ASSERT NOT `the taxpayer is a legal foreign worker in the caring sector` `a legal foreign man whose stay is extended but who has no caring-sector permit, an Israeli resident`

-- Not reached by either instrument: the ordinary sections govern, not decided here.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a foreign man who needs no visa` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `an Israeli citizen who works in Israel` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a worker who is a resident of Israel under the Foreign Workers Law` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer`

§§ `A foreign worker who is an Israeli resident — the Regulations' points`

-- Caring sector, man: REG 3(a): s 34 = 2, s 36 = 1/4, s 36A = 0 (not a woman). s 37: REG 3(d) disapplies it, 0.
-- Total 2 + 1/4 = 9/4. Whole year, 12 months: 12/12 = 1.
#ASSERT `s34` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s36` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `s36A` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s37` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4
-- Caring sector, woman: 2 + 1/4 + 1/2 = 11/4.
#ASSERT `s36A` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 11/4
-- Other legal foreign man: REG 3(a1): one point under s 34 only. 1.
#ASSERT `s34` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s36` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1
-- Other legal foreign woman: REG 3(a1) one point + REG 3(b) half a point under s 36A: 1 + 1/2 = 3/2.
#ASSERT `s36A` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 3/2
-- A caring-sector permit without the s 3A(b) extension (or the extension without the permit) is not the caring sector: 1.
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man with a caring-sector permit whose stay is not extended, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man whose stay is extended but who has no caring-sector permit, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1

§§ `Not a legal foreign worker, or other income — REG 3(d) takes the rest away`

-- A foreign worker who is not a legal one is still a foreign worker (REG 1), so REG 3(d) disapplies the chapter's
-- credits and the Regulations give him nothing. Not a refusal: the law's own answer. 0.
#ASSERT `total` `a foreign man who holds no B/1 visa` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a foreign man who is an expert from abroad` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a foreign man with a B/1 visa whose stay is not permitted by law` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
-- REG 3(a) gives points in computing tax on income under s 2(1) or (2); on other income REG 3(d) leaves none.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, an Israeli resident, taxed on other income` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0

§§ `A foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident (fork FW1)`

-- Reading A: the Regulations give their points without the cited sections' residence conditions. B: s 34 and s 36 still
-- need an Israeli resident, and s 36A its own condition (fork F1). D: declined where they differ.
-- Caring man: A 2 + 1/4 = 9/4.  B: 0 + 0 + 0 = 0.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s34` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B` EQUALS 0
-- Caring woman: A 11/4.  B with F1 B (36A only for Israeli residents): 0.  B with F1 A (no residence condition): 0 + 0 + 1/2 = 1/2.
-- B with F1 declined: s 36A refuses on F1.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A` EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B and F1 is B` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B and F1 is A` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36A` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B and F1 is D` BECAUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"
-- Other legal man: A 1.  B 0.
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B` EQUALS 0
-- Other legal woman: A 1 + 1/2 = 3/2.  B with F1 B: 0.
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A` EQUALS 3/2
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is B and F1 is B` EQUALS 0
-- Where the readings agree the default answers: s 36A for a non-resident legal woman with FW1 declined but F1 = A:
-- reading A of FW1 gives 1/2, reading B of FW1 with F1 = A gives 1/2.
#ASSERT `s36A` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but F1 is A` EQUALS 1/2
-- ... but with F1 = B the two disagree (1/2 against 0), and with F1 declined likewise.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36A` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but F1 is B` BECAUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36A` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"
-- s 36 for a non-resident caring man with no income from personal exertion: with F2 = B both FW1 readings give 0, so the
-- default (FW1 declined) answers 0; with F2 declined the quarter point's own question is unanswered.
#ASSERT `s36` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but F2 is B` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"
-- Most generous and least generous readings, all forks at once.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the readings that give the most` EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, not an Israeli resident` `under` `the readings that give the least` EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 36 and income from personal exertion (fork F2), for a foreign worker`

-- Resident caring man without such income. D: s 36 declined. A: 1/4, total 9/4. B: 0, total 2.
#ASSERT `s34` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `s36` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but F2 is A` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man without income from personal exertion, an Israeli resident` `under` `the default readings but F2 is B` EQUALS 2

§§ `A stay for part of the tax year — REG 3(c)`

-- 1/12 of the points x the months. Caring man 6 months: (2 + 1/4) x 6/12 = 9/8; s 34 = 1, s 36 = 1/8.
#ASSERT `s34` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s36` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 1/8
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/8
-- Caring woman 6 months: 11/4 x 6/12 = 11/8.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, an Israeli resident, for 6 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 11/8
-- Other legal man 9 months: 1 x 9/12 = 3/4.
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident, for 9 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 3/4
-- 0 months: 0.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for 0 months` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 0
-- A count outside 0 to 12 is not a number of months of a year.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for 13 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the months spent in Israel or the Area must be a whole number from 0 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, for -1 months` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the months spent in Israel or the Area must be a whole number from 0 to 12"

§§ `The tax years`

-- REG 4: income produced in 2015 or after. The deposited text is the consolidation after the amendments of 5777 and 5778
-- (heading of reg 3), so it is held from 2019 (the rule row IL-01 uses, its fork F12); 2015 to 2018 need the text as made.
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2019` `under` `the default readings` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2018` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds the Regulations as they stood only from the tax year 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2015` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "this encoding holds the Regulations as they stood only from the tax year 2019"
-- 2002 to 2014: s 48A exists (enacted in 5763) but the Regulations do not yet apply (REG 4); fork FW2.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2014` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Regulations start with the tax year 2015 and whether an instrument under section 48A applied from 2002 to 2014 is not in the sources"
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2002` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the Regulations start with the tax year 2015 and whether an instrument under section 48A applied from 2002 to 2014 is not in the sources"
-- Reading A: no instrument applied; the ordinary sections govern, which this row does not decide.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2014` `under` `the default readings but FW2 is A` BECAUSE "neither the Area order nor the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, so the ordinary sections govern and are not decided here"
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2014` `, under` `the default readings but FW2 is A` EQUALS `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`
-- Before 2002 s 48A did not exist (enacted in 5763): no instrument under any reading.
#ASSERT `the instrument that reaches` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident, in 2001` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `neither instrument reaches the taxpayer`

§§ `What the Regulations do to each provision of Chapter Three — REG 3(d)`

-- ss 34, 36 and 36A: a partial effect, the points above. Every other credit section: disapplied.
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 34` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 36` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 36A` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `gives the provision a partial effect, set out in the points`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 37` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 40` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 35` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 45A` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 46` `, under` `the default readings` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
-- The two deduction sections: REG 3(d) says "the provisions of Chapter Three", s 48A's power says credits (fork FW3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `what the Regulations do to` `section 47, a deduction` `, under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "regulation 3(d) speaks of the whole chapter but section 48A's power speaks of credits, so whether it reaches the chapter's deductions is not decided"
#ASSERT REFUSED `what the Regulations do to` `section 47A, a deduction` `, under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "regulation 3(d) speaks of the whole chapter but section 48A's power speaks of credits, so whether it reaches the chapter's deductions is not decided"
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 47, a deduction` `, under` `the default readings but FW3 is A` EQUALS `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 47A, a deduction` `, under` `the default readings but FW3 is B` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
-- A credit section is disapplied on every reading of FW3.
#ASSERT `what the Regulations do to` `section 40` `, under` `the default readings but FW3 is A` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`
#ASSERT `what the instrument that reaches` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, does to` `section 40` EQUALS `disapplies the provision`

§§ `A foreign worker who is also a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen (fork OV)`

-- Both instruments reach him: the Order applies ss 34, 36, 37; REG 3(d) takes the chapter's provisions from him.
-- Default: declined. OV A (regulations prevail, FW1 A): other legal man: s 34 = 1, total 1. OV B (the Order prevails):
-- an Area man: 2 + 1/4 = 9/4.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "both the Area order and the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, and the sources do not say which prevails"
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A and OV is A` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `total` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings but FW1 is A and OV is B` EQUALS 9/4
-- A foreign worker who is not a legal one and an Area resident: the Regulations give 0, the Order 9/4.
#ASSERT REFUSED `total` `a foreign man who needs a visa but is not legal, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings` BECAUSE "both the Area order and the foreign worker regulations reach the taxpayer, and the sources do not say which prevails"
#ASSERT `total` `a foreign man who needs a visa but is not legal, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings but OV is A` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `total` `a foreign man who needs a visa but is not legal, who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the default readings but OV is B` EQUALS 9/4
-- Most generous (Order prevails, 9/4 for a caring man) and least (regulations prevail, FW1 B: 0 for a non-resident).
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the readings that give the most` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `total` `a caring-sector legal foreign man who is also a resident of the Area and not an Israeli citizen` `under` `the readings that give the least` EQUALS 0

§§ `The amount in NIS`

-- Illustrative input only: NIS 2,904 per credit point (row IL-01's published figure for 2025; not law).
-- 9/4 x 2904 = 6534.  11/4 x 2904 = 7986.  1 x 2904 = 2904.  3/2 x 2904 = 4356.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `a caring-sector legal foreign woman, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `a legal foreign man, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `a legal foreign woman, not in the caring sector, an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 EQUALS 4356
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount of the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` `a caring-sector legal foreign man, not an Israeli resident` `, under` `the default readings` `, at` 2904 BECAUSE "the Regulations do not say whether the cited sections' residence conditions bind a foreign worker who is not an Israeli resident"
